{
  "spec": "content/notes/design-spec.md §12.2 — one row per output id.",
  "notes": [
    "crop is in source pixels (left, top, width, height). Every box was opened at native resolution and tightened until it holds the object and nothing else: no slide text, no neighbouring tile, no panel border.",
    "out is the size src/content/*.ts declares for the id (ImageRef.width/height). The crop is centred on a ground-coloured canvas of that aspect and then downscaled to it, so the object is never enlarged and never stretched.",
    "ground: dark = level the near-black ground onto --bg #0B0E13 (measured ground level -> token, 255 stays 255); light = level the border median to --plate-light #E6E7E9; photo = keep the photograph's own ground. Padding uses the same tone, so the canvas seam does not exist.",
    "cleared: false means the file is built into the QA directory for review and is NOT written to public/."
  ],
  "defaults": {
    "bg": "#0B0E13",
    "plateLight": "#E6E7E9",
    "jpgQuality": 90,
    "webpQuality": 90,
    "avifQuality": 62
  },
